`splitInstructions` partitions instructions into query and command arrays while preserving relative input order within each group. Empty input returns two empty arrays. Inputs are treated as immutable and must not be reordered or modified. Every returned instruction, including its `arguments` array, must be detached from the input and from all other returned objects; later mutations must not cross aliases. The discriminated union is exhaustive.

